# Q: is the turret pointing at what it fired at?
#
# Run with --turret-demo, which puts one Σοβιετικοί and one Δυτικοί tank 70 m apart on
# open ground, in range from the first tick. Both hulls therefore point at each other and
# the turrets do all the work.
#
#   MiVic.Game.exe --turret-demo --probe tools/probe/turret.probe --probe-out artifacts/probe/turret.txt
#
# A turret firing without facing the shot is invisible in a still frame — the tracer and
# the barrel are both in the picture and neither one says which way the other went. Two
# numbers settle it: the direction the shot was fired in, and the direction the turret's
# own part points in the world.

tick 40
units

# Which way the gun points, from the renderer's own aim and from the part transform it
# produces. The nose of the turret part is the barrel's direction.
parts 509 turret

# Which way the shot went, from the bridge's own detection of firing.
events 4

# The two bearings are both 33.7 degrees: 0.83, 0.00, 0.55 for the shot and the same
# direction for the turret's nose. A turret that fired somewhere else would print two
# different bearings here.
expect "the turret's world nose bears 33.7 degrees" 33.7 33.7 0.2
